From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the Recycle Bin folder and its menu, SHCreateFileExtractIconW (3700)

shell32: the Recycle Bin folder and its menu, SHCreateFileExtractIconW

The menu of a Recycle Bin item answered QueryInterface with E_NOTIMPL, so
nothing could ask it for IContextMenu2 or even IUnknown; it now returns
itself for IUnknown, IContextMenu and IContextMenu2 and E_NOINTERFACE for the
rest. Its QueryContextMenu no longer leaks the menu resource and adds
nothing, with success, for CMF_DEFAULTONLY. GetCommandString gives the verbs
(undelete, delete), their help text and validates commands by number or
verb name; HandleMenuMsg takes the menu messages that need no work.

The folder itself: ParseDisplayName finds an item by its name in the bin or
by the path it was deleted from; BindToObject opens a deleted folder where
it lies in the trash; BindToStorage gives the stream of a deleted file;
GetUIObjectOf gives the icon of the item and refuses unknown objects with
E_NOINTERFACE (it dereferenced a missing item list); GetDetailsEx gives
typed values (size as 64-bit integer, dates as variant dates) and the
column texts; CompareIDs orders by the column asked for, then by name,
instead of comparing the raw bytes of the item. SHUpdateRecycleBinIcon tells
the views of the bin to update the item.

SHCreateFileExtractIconW, which the Recycle Bin uses, was a stub: it now
makes the default icon extractor for a file name and its attributes
(IExtractIconA or IExtractIconW).
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/recyclebin.c b/dlls/shell32/recyclebin.c
index 7867f1b..cb5eaaf 100644
